.TH SELEVER 1 "2026-07-30" "Selever" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
selever \- install an exact toolchain or package and print its shell environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B node
.I version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B npm
.I package@version
.BI \-\-node= version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B go
.I version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B gopkg
.I package@version
.BI \-\-go= version
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B msvc
.I version
.RB [ \-\-host=\fIarch\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-target=\fIarch\fR ]
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B winsdk
.I build
.RB [ \-\-host=\fIarch\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-target=\fIarch\fR ]
.br
.B selever
.RI [ \-\-shell= shell ]
.B batch
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B selever
installs the selected toolchain or package in an immutable directory and writes
the shell code needed to add its executables to
.BR PATH .
MSVC and the Windows SDK also set
.BR INCLUDE ,
.BR LIB ,
and related variables.
Progress and diagnostics are written to standard error.
.PP
All versions passed to
.B selever
must be exact.
Package installations are identified by both the package version and the parent
toolchain version.
Completed installations are reused without network access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "node " version
Install an exact Node.js release.
The version must not have a leading
.BR v .
.TP
.BI "npm " package@version " \-\-node=" version
Install an exact npm package using the specified exact Node.js release.
.TP
.BI "go " version
Install an exact Go release.
The version must not have a leading
.BR go .
.TP
.BI "gopkg " package@version " \-\-go=" version
Build and install an exact Go package using the specified exact Go release.
A leading
.B v
on the module version is optional.
.TP
.BI "msvc " version
Install an exact MSVC toolset (Windows only).
.I version
is the toolset version in the Visual Studio package id, such as
.B 14.44.17.14
or
.BR 14.51 .
The toolset is the compiler for one host and one target architecture, its
C and C++ runtime headers and libraries, ASan, PGO, and the debug runtime DLLs.
It does not include the Windows SDK; install it with
.BR winsdk .
.TP
.BI "winsdk " build
Install an exact Windows SDK (Windows only).
.I build
is the SDK build number, such as
.BR 26100 .
The SDK has the headers, the import libraries for the target, and the tools
.RB ( rc ,
.BR mt ,
\&...) for the host.
The MSIs are unpacked with
.BR "msiexec /a" ,
which needs no elevation.
.TP
.B batch
Read selectors from standard input and emit one environment update.
See
.BR "BATCH INPUT" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-shell= shell
Select the format written to standard output.
Accepted values are
.BR auto ,
.BR sh ,
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.BR pwsh ,
.BR powershell ,
.BR nu ,
and
.BR nushell .
The default is
.BR auto ,
which detects the invoking shell and falls back to
.BR sh .
.TP
.BI \-\-host= arch
For
.B msvc
and
.BR winsdk ,
the architecture the tools run on:
.BR x64 ,
.BR x86 ,
or
.BR arm64 .
The default is the native architecture.
.TP
.BI \-\-target= arch
For
.B msvc
and
.BR winsdk ,
the architecture to build for:
.BR x64 ,
.BR x86 ,
.BR arm ,
or
.BR arm64 .
The default is the host.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.SH BATCH INPUT
.B selever batch
reads one selector per line: a
.BR node ,
.BR npm ,
.BR go ,
.BR gopkg ,
.BR msvc ,
or
.B winsdk
command with the same arguments and options as above, without
.BR selever .
.B \-\-shell
is given once, to
.BR "selever batch" .
Fields are separated by whitespace; quoting is not supported.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
Processing stops at the first failing line.
The final environment update combines the updates of every line, in input
order.
.PP
.EX
selever batch <<'EOF'
go 1.18
gopkg --go=1.18 golang.org/x/tools/gopls@0.14.2
EOF
.EE
.PP
List
.B msvc
before
.B winsdk
so the MSVC headers come first in
.BR INCLUDE :
.PP
.EX
selever batch <<'EOF'
msvc --target=x86 14.44.17.14
winsdk --target=x86 26100
EOF
.EE
.SH OUTPUT
For sh, bash, and zsh,
.B selever
writes an
.B export PATH=
command.
For fish it writes a
.B set \-gx PATH
command, and for PowerShell it writes an assignment to
.BR $env:PATH .
Other list variables, such as
.BR INCLUDE ,
are prepended in the same way with the platform's list separator, and other
variables are assigned.
For Nushell it writes a JSON object whose
.B PATH
is the complete new search path as a list, suitable for
.BR load-env .
Other list variables are strings holding the new entries followed by the
inherited value:
.PP
.EX
selever node 22.14.0 | from json | load-env
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate default data and cache directories.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the data directory base.
The default is
.BR $HOME/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Overrides the cache directory base.
The default is
.BR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B SHELL
Used as a fallback when automatic shell detection cannot identify the parent
process.
.TP
.B HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY
Control proxies for HTTP metadata and download requests.
.TP
.B GOPROXY
Controls module lookup while installing Go packages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/selever
Immutable toolchain and package installations.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:\-$HOME/.cache}/selever
Downloaded metadata and archives.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B selever
exits with status 0 after the selection is installed and the environment update
is written.
It exits non-zero if its arguments or batch input are invalid, shell detection
is overridden with an unsupported value, or an installation fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install Node.js 22.14.0 and print its environment update:
.PP
.EX
selever node 22.14.0
.EE
.PP
Install TypeScript 5.8.2 using Node.js 22.14.0:
.PP
.EX
selever npm typescript@5.8.2 --node 22.14.0
.EE
.PP
Resolve a non-exact version before installing it:
.PP
.EX
selever node "$(fetchver node 22)"
.EE
.PP
Install the latest MSVC and Windows SDK in Nushell:
.PP
.EX
$"msvc (fetchver msvc latest)\\nwinsdk (fetchver winsdk latest)\\n"
| selever batch | from json | load-env
.EE
.SH NOTES
Node.js and Go archives and MSVC and Windows SDK payloads are
checksum-verified.
MSVC and the Windows SDK are downloaded from the Visual Studio 2026 stable
channel manifest, which also lists the Visual Studio 2019 and 2022 toolsets.
The manifest is cached and refetched only when a requested version is missing
from it.
npm retains its native integrity and lifecycle behavior.
Installations are completed in a staging directory and moved into place
atomically while holding an exclusive lock for the installation identity.
.PP
Supported platforms are macOS, glibc Linux, and Windows on amd64 and arm64.
On Windows, Node.js executables are in the installation root rather than
.IR bin ,
and
.B HOME
is read from
.BR USERPROFILE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fetchver (1),
.BR globver (1)
